## Findings, severity ordered

### P2 — Specify the conditional integration target/proposal and approximation-error acceptance before approving its implementation

Location: `docs/implementation/g1-technical-plan-20261021.md:75-79,103,111`.
Requirements: `docs/implementation/dgp-decisions.md:30,89,93`; `docs/spec/dgp-reference.md:34,44,52-58,64-66`.

The selected method is sequential importance/resampling over structural latent state, with ESS/resampling/normalization diagnostics and independent-batch MCSE. This does not yet define a feasible conditional-truth algorithm or a sufficient accuracy criterion. The plan itself says its proposal/diagnostics still require critique; this review cannot treat that unresolved design as an accepted method merely because failures will be labeled unresolved.

The actual conditioning law matters here. Current pain is an exact continuous observation of a coordinate of L, not a noisy measurement. A prior-transition particle proposal weighted by equality to the observed pain has zero support almost surely. It needs an explicit conditional proposal/analytic conditioning or equivalent justified construction. Daily quality/function/wearable clipping creates boundary atoms; ISI uses shared recall, overlapping windows and, in a stress, correlated items. Observed assignment, reporting/nonreporting, interruption and delayed-arrival history can also carry information about latent state (including withheld U). A filter conditioned only on observed symptom values would target a different conditional distribution even if its weights look stable. These are concrete properties of the already accepted DGP, not speculative extra scenarios.

There is a second, distinct problem: self-normalized finite-particle estimates can have bias that does not disappear by averaging more independent filters at the same particle budget. The batch MCSE then becomes arbitrarily small around the wrong limit. ESS, normalized weights and a resampling log do not bound that approximation error. A simple analytic illustration is a binary latent state with prior probability 1/2 and observation likelihoods .1/.9: the posterior probability is .9, but a one-particle self-normalized estimator averages to .5 over arbitrarily many independent runs. Its ESS is always maximal for its particle count and its batch MCSE tends to zero. This illustration does not claim the proposed production budget is one particle; it demonstrates why the proposed diagnostics alone cannot certify truth.

Requested bounded revision: state the conditioning variables/factorization, latent state retained across time/recall, handling of exact observations and clipped atoms, and how observed assignment/reporting/arrival/interruptions enter or are legitimately ancillary. Select a concrete evaluator-only proposal/resampling approach and particle-budget/refinement policy, with independently testable accuracy criteria that distinguish integration approximation error from rollout MCSE. Name the initial mandatory conditional targets/scenarios and where unresolved conditional work blocks acceptance versus remains a later comparator dependency. Reduced analytic/discrete examples should include informative observation/assignment and an exact-observation case, with fault detection for omitted likelihood factors. No alternative live Bayesian backend or broad inference framework is requested.

### P2 — Close the pre-G2 estimator-SE dependency for S10 solved calibration bindings

Location: `docs/implementation/g1-technical-plan-20261021.md:79,83-87,107,111`.
Contract: `contracts/dgp/calibration.py:ExternalTargetEvidence`, `CalibrationBinding.precision_and_provenance`, `require_solved`; `docs/implementation/dgp-decisions.md:79-81,93`.

The plan specifies the source-scale pilot precisely: 1,000 randomized n200 trials and sqrt(mean(SE_j^2)). It does not identify the independently piloted *comparator estimator SE* needed for the separate `smallest_estimator_se` field and relative truth criterion. The source-scale pilot is not automatically that comparator; it sets the S10 shift magnitude. The plan allows relative precision to remain pending until later comparator results, yet also requires every S10 cell's solved binding before execution and all 82 cells for G1 acceptance.

This is a concrete dependency gap rather than a complaint that future results are absent. With source reference, source SE and source-SE MCSE available but no independently piloted comparator SE, `ExternalTargetEvidence` cannot be constructed with an absent value, external CalibrationBinding cannot become solved, and `require_solved` cannot yield the coefficient. An arbitrary positive placeholder would defeat the precision contract. Waiting for a G2 estimator whose data depend on G1 leaves the stated execution order unresolved. The existing source pilot could contribute an appropriate comparator only if that comparator, target and use are explicitly defined and justified; its existence alone does not establish equivalence.

Requested bounded revision: name the pre-G2 G1 comparison estimator(s), population/horizon/sample sizes and independent pilot recipe used to obtain the smallest relevant SE for source calibration, with artifact identity and uncertainty handling. Explain its relationship to the n200 source-shift scale and why it is appropriate for the G1 comparison. Keep later matched G2/G4 SE tightening as a separate recorded dependency. State that pending later refinement never relaxes the solved S10 binding requirement. If this cannot be supplied within the approved contract, explicitly resolve the dependency/contract proposal before dispatch rather than weakening the binding or inventing a generous SE.

## Assessed areas without additional plan blockers

The accepted LIB merge resolves the plan's formerly pending library dependency; its candidate wording was correct at creation. Refresh the dependency status and exact integration base when Sol incorporates the revised plan. No new library-selection work or repeated native-NUTS/R/BCF fit is needed for this critique. Final integration must receive refreshed exact-head/base review on current main, as root requested.

Foundation design is suitably bounded: one FastAPI process, SQLite WAL/foreign keys/FULL synchronization, explicit transaction/migration ownership, no extra distributed framework. Atomic approval/state/audit/idempotency/cursor writes, rollback and racing hold/consent/version tests address meaningful failure modes. Cutoff-first lineage projection and persisted display payloads preserve historical decisions. Reversed replay must use declared source chronology; live receipts remain actual receipt times. Session revocation, ownership before aggregates, nested-resource checks, CSRF, reset invalidation and same-doctor reauthentication tests are explicit. Exact auth/runtime settings and release qualification are ordinary implementation decisions already assigned to integration, not additional independent plan blockers.

Truth isolation uses actual separate images/identities/mounts and export admission, excludes privileged source/parameters from consumers, and requires negative probes plus a positive evaluator canary. This is materially stronger than field-name filtering or module naming. It correctly treats host administrator as trusted. Actual Docker/mount/network/static/debug behavior remains future acceptance evidence; no source-only claim substitutes for it.

The thin shell supports ordinary synthetic care, all ASSIGN-state permission/status displays and immutable history while refusing unavailable engines and invented model outputs. Its browser requirements cover persisted backend behavior, identity races and history reload. Detailed UI skills, rendered review, full integrated stories and manual/human accessibility remain assigned future obligations; this plan critique is not a UI-code review.

Generator/evaluator ownership and equation independence are explicit. Layer A reductions, separate intervention transition code, descendant/sign/continuation faults and paired null tests preserve the accepted causal requirements. The timing plan preserves independent pain on missing-report days, strict arrival cutoffs, distinct report/wearable delay origins, and named RNG substreams. The prescribed seeds/versions and process-level denial are not represented as already executed.

The 82-cell/73-variant/32-family catalog, explicit n60/n240 restriction, deterministic fault cells and smoke/demonstration presets are retained without replacing cell n by preset n. Five repetitions per executable cell exceed the per-family smoke minimum without waiving later 200/1000/2000-run requirements. Model-dependent cells retain input/fault evidence and pending later inference rather than claiming engines exist. External summaries derive from actual trials and prohibit duplicate summary/IPD likelihood use.

Resource reality remains a risk, not evidence that the plan is infeasible: a 200,000-patient longitudinal calibration sample alone represents roughly twenty million patient-days, and 10,000-by-1,000 truth draws can be expensive across targets. Existing batching, caps, atomic checkpoints, retained failed runs and bulk storage are appropriate. During scaffolding, measure generator/truth throughput and memory/storage on a small representative batch before full calibration, estimate the required jobs, and retain the estimate with commands; do not lower required samples to meet a guessed budget. This is execution planning, not a third approval blocker or permission to replace the separate required 20-fit G2 pilot.

